{"kind":"assert","text":"R13 item 4 rulings, restated live on request 90878601. My 8 November cleanup closed question e0f5676d as answered, and that left ruling f21e5c62 stale, along with question b2e3e5a6 and my answer 9958fc1e. This act carries all of them. Nothing in them changes.\n\nFrom f21e5c62, the member read-token quota:\n1. One bucket per member, keyed by the authenticated membership ScopeRef and member identity, inside each destination object. Several keys of one member share it. No global bucket, and no bucket across incarnations.\n2. At most 8 open tokens per bucket. Reserve the slot durably and atomically before the provider call.\n3. A slot is open from its reservation until the token's actual expiresAt. Taking or dropping the plaintext does not free it. An explicit minted:false frees it at once.\n4. Unknown mint: count the slot as open until the reservation time plus the requested hours plus 10 minutes, then free it. The docs say that the quota counts reservations and is not proof that a provider token ended.\n5. Legacy read markers with no member identity belong to no bucket: they neither count nor get cleaned up by caller key or handle prefix.\n6. The 1-to-24-hour request contract stays.\n\nFrom 9958fc1e, the refusal boundary asked in b2e3e5a6:\n7. Refuse the fresh mint act at the native commit with the reason `limit`, after the held membership authority identifies the member and before any operation entry is accepted. A refused act records nothing.\n8. The mint-read outcome keeps its pinned meaning, and no historical destination pin changes.\n9. Reserve the slot in the same transaction as the accepted operation entry. The adapter binds and updates it around the provider call.\n10. A retry of an already accepted key returns its existing receipt or mismatch and never counts a second slot.\n11. Witness: the ninth open mint of one member is refused `limit` with no entry, and another member's mint in the same destination succeeds.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}